# =============================================================================
# CLINE RULES CONFIGURATION - Budgeteer Project
# =============================================================================
# This file defines rules for how Cline should work with this project.
# Everything in this file (including comments) is read as instructions.

# =============================================================================
# 📚 PROJECT CONTEXT & DOCUMENTATION
# =============================================================================
# These files are automatically included in Cline's context window

@context .docs/docs/api/monzo-api.pdf
@context .docs/docs/project/PROJECT.md
@context .docs/docs/project/ARCHITECTURE.md
@context .docs/docs/project/DEVELOPMENT-PLAN.md
@context .docs/docs/project/MONZO-AUTH-FLOW.md
@context .docs/notes/cline-memory.md

# Files to read at the start of tasks to understand project state
@read .docs/docs/project/PROJECT.md
@read .docs/docs/project/ARCHITECTURE.md
@read .docs/notes/cline-memory.md

# =============================================================================
# 📁 PROJECT STRUCTURE
# =============================================================================
# This is a MONO-REPO with the following structure:
# 
# budgeteer/
# ├── backend/              (Spring Boot API - to be moved here)
# ├── frontend/             (React/Vue/etc - future)
# ├── src/                  (Current Spring Boot location)
# ├── .docs/                (Documentation - git-ignored)
# │   ├── docs/api/         - API references (Monzo, our API)
# │   ├── docs/project/     - Project planning & architecture
# │   └── notes/            - Working notes, scratch files
# └── docs/                 (Public docs - to be created later)

# =============================================================================
# 🎯 WORKING GUIDELINES
# =============================================================================
# When working on this project, Cline should:

# PROJECT MANAGEMENT
# 1. Always refer to PROJECT.md for overall project goals and current status
# 2. Check ARCHITECTURE.md before making significant architectural changes
# 3. Reference DEVELOPMENT-PLAN.md for the current phase and priorities
# 4. Update cline-memory.md with important decisions and context for future sessions

# MONZO API INTEGRATION
# 5. Reference monzo-api.pdf when implementing Monzo API integrations
# 6. Follow MONZO-AUTH-FLOW.md for OAuth implementation details
# 7. Never log or expose access tokens or refresh tokens

# =============================================================================
# 💻 CODE STYLE & STANDARDS
# =============================================================================

# JAVA/SPRING BOOT
# - Follow Google Java Style Guide
# - Use meaningful, descriptive variable and method names
# - Add Javadoc comments for all public classes and methods
# - Use constructor injection over field injection for dependencies
# - Keep controllers thin - business logic belongs in services
# - Use DTOs for API requests/responses, not entities directly

# PACKAGE STRUCTURE
# - dev.amf.budgeteer.controller   - REST controllers
# - dev.amf.budgeteer.service      - Business logic
# - dev.amf.budgeteer.repository   - Data access
# - dev.amf.budgeteer.model        - Entities and DTOs
# - dev.amf.budgeteer.config       - Configuration classes
# - dev.amf.budgeteer.exception    - Custom exceptions
# - dev.amf.budgeteer.client       - External API clients (Monzo)

# =============================================================================
# 🧪 TESTING REQUIREMENTS
# =============================================================================

# When writing new code:
# - Write unit tests for all service methods
# - Use @WebMvcTest for controller tests
# - Use @DataJpaTest for repository tests  
# - Use @SpringBootTest sparingly (integration tests only)
# - Mock external services (Monzo API) in tests
# - Aim for meaningful test coverage, not 100% line coverage

# =============================================================================
# 🔀 GIT WORKFLOW
# =============================================================================

# BRANCHING
# - main          - Production-ready code
# - develop       - Integration branch (if used)
# - feature/*     - New features (e.g., feature/monzo-oauth)
# - fix/*         - Bug fixes
# - refactor/*    - Code improvements

# COMMITS - Use Conventional Commits
# - feat:     New feature (feat: add transaction sync endpoint)
# - fix:      Bug fix (fix: handle null account balance)
# - docs:     Documentation (docs: update API documentation)
# - refactor: Code refactoring (refactor: extract MonzoClient)
# - test:     Test additions (test: add UserService unit tests)
# - chore:    Maintenance (chore: update dependencies)

# =============================================================================
# 📋 COMMON TASK TEMPLATES
# =============================================================================

# When asked to "add a new REST endpoint":
# 1. Create/update controller with the endpoint
# 2. Add service layer method with business logic
# 3. Create/update repository if data access needed
# 4. Create request/response DTOs if needed
# 5. Write unit tests for service and controller
# 6. Update API documentation

# When asked to "add a new entity":
# 1. Create entity class with JPA annotations
# 2. Create repository interface
# 3. Add Flyway migration for the table
# 4. Create DTOs for API exposure
# 5. Add to ARCHITECTURE.md if significant

# When asked to "integrate with Monzo API":
# 1. Check monzo-api.pdf for endpoint details
# 2. Check MONZO-AUTH-FLOW.md for auth requirements
# 3. Add method to MonzoClient
# 4. Create appropriate DTOs
# 5. Handle rate limits and errors gracefully

# =============================================================================
# ⚡ AUTO-APPROVE COMMANDS
# =============================================================================
# These commands run without asking for approval each time.
# Uncomment the ones you want to auto-approve.

@auto-approve mvn clean install -DskipTests
@auto-approve mvn spring-boot:run
@auto-approve mvn test
# @auto-approve mvn clean install
# @auto-approve docker-compose up -d
# @auto-approve docker-compose down

# =============================================================================
# 🧠 SESSION MEMORY
# =============================================================================
# At the end of significant work sessions, update .docs/notes/cline-memory.md with:
# - Decisions made and their rationale
# - Current state of work in progress
# - Known issues or TODOs
# - Any context that would help future sessions

# =============================================================================
